[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5570711618","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123272#issuecomment-5570711618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123272","id":5570711618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTApQQg","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:34:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T12:34:53Z","body":"Sorry I'm not that familiar with how that part works to know if the fix is fully correct, but it looks fine.\r\n\r\nCreated WebSocket adds a callback to `GodotWebSocket._onmessage` that is called by the browser on the [event](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebSocket/message_event) that is then directly calls `EMWSPeer::_esws_on_message` so users can't even use `Mutex` themselves to prevent the data race. This seems like the only solution if we want to be able to call `get_packet` from another thread easily. And it seems not worth it to try to create some sort of lock-free structure here. Same reasoning extends for other methods.","author_asso